{
  "name": "Colonnades",
  "_about": "A COLONNADE is columns and what they carry: base, shaft (tapering to `taper` of its foot), capital (the flare and the square abacus on it) and the entablature, set out STRAIGHT at a `spacing` or ROUND on a `radius` -- a whole ring (a tholos, a rotunda's peristyle) or an `arc` of one with a column at each end (Bernini's arms round St Peter's square). A round entablature is a ring with one bay per column, so its joints fall between them.",
